# GLM-5.1-int4-mixed-AutoRound  —  fused-MoE single-stream lazy + FP8 KV CACHE
# ============================================================================
# Item 3 of the MoE-ext fp8 work: the ORTHOGONAL fp8 toggle. This is a SERVING
# flag (--kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc), NOT a kernel change — it quantizes the KV
# cache to fp8, it does NOT touch the int4 MoE op or the fp8-COMPUTE op variant.
# Base config is glm51ar-lazy.env (the coherent single-stream lazy path: fused
# int4 MoE via HPU_MOE_ROUTED_K=8, repack-cache load, the GLM coherence fixes);
# the ONLY adds here are the FP8-KV flag + its INC calibration env.
#
# >>> WHAT IT BUYS / DOES NOT BUY <<<
#   WIN : ~2x KV headroom (fp8 KV bytes ~= 1/2 bf16). A CONTEXT / MEMORY lever —
#         longer max-model-len and/or more concurrent sequences in the same HBM.
#         For GLM's MLA this is the LATENT KV (kv_lora_rank-wide), already small,
#         so the absolute saving is smaller than a dense-KV model's, but real.
#   ~0  : single-stream tok/s. Decode at batch=1 is weight-bandwidth bound (the
#         all-expert/int4 dequant floor); halving KV bytes does ~nothing for it
#         (Gaudi2_Kernel/SPEED_MASTER_PLAN.md L7: "~0 single-stream, ~2x KV").
#   So use this profile to PUSH CONTEXT/CONCURRENCY, not latency. The single-
#   stream speed work stays in glm51ar-lazy.env + the fused/fp8-compute op.
#
# ============================================================================
# REQUIREMENT 1 — fp8_inc is the ONLY accepted KV dtype on Gaudi, and it is INC.
# ============================================================================
# The HPU platform gate (is_kv_cache_dtype_supported) returns True ONLY for
# "fp8_inc" — not "fp8", not "fp8_e4m3" (vendor/platform_PR1301.py:308-309). INC
# (Intel Neural Compressor) is the master switch: it is driven by QUANT_CONFIG
# (a JSON), NOT by a bare --quantization flag. Two cases:
#
#   (a) MEASURE-FREE default scales — INC can run KV-only fp8 with its built-in
#       per-tensor dynamic scaling and needs no calibration JSON for the KV cache
#       ITSELF in some builds (the kv quant uses runtime maxabs). If this build
#       accepts --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc with NO QUANT_CONFIG, the env below works
#       as-is (QUANT_CONFIG left UNSET). VERIFY on the box: a startup line
#       confirming fp8_inc KV + no INC-config error.
#
#   (b) CALIBRATED scales (recommended for quality) — mint a Gaudi-2 maxabs config
#       and point QUANT_CONFIG at it. ON the g2 cards (never reuse Gaudi3 scales:
#       ±240 fnuz vs ±448 fn -> clip):
#         vllm-hpu-extension/calibration/calibrate_model.sh -o g2 \
#             -m GLM-5.1-int4-mixed-AutoRound ...
#       (MEASURE -> maxabs_measure_g2.json, QUANTIZE -> maxabs_quant_g2.json).
#       Then add to MODEL_ENV: -e QUANT_CONFIG=/models/maxabs_quant_g2.json
#       NEVER scale_method=unit_scale (Mixtral PPL 11.34->96.65). Use maxabs.
#       (Gaudi2_Optimization_Guide.md §4 + §Part-III.)
#   The QUANT_CONFIG line is COMMENTED in MODEL_ENV below — uncomment after minting
#   the g2 calibration if quality needs it (start with (a), A/B vs bf16 KV).
#
# ============================================================================
# REQUIREMENT 2 — MLA-LATENT-KV fp8 COHERENCE CHECK (GLM & DeepSeek use MLA).
# ============================================================================
# GLM-5.1 (GlmMoeDsa) and DeepSeek-V3 attention is MLA: the KV cache is the
# COMPRESSED latent (kv_lora_rank-wide), NOT per-head K/V. On HPU the fp8 KV path
# for MLA is a SEPARATE code path from dense attention:
#   HPUCompressedTensorsKVCacheMethodForMLA (reference/hpu_compressed_tensors.py:1048)
#   scales ONLY layer.impl.latent_cache_k (input_scale=k_scale, output_scale=1/k_scale)
#   — there is NO separate v_cache: the latent already absorbs V (kv_b_proj expands
#   it per-head at read). So the fp8 quant lands on the latent-K BEFORE the up-
#   projection, and the up-projected per-head V inherits that fp8 error.
# COHERENCE RISK + GATE (run on the box, do NOT trust tok/s before it is clean):
#   1. Generate with this profile vs glm51ar-lazy.env (bf16 KV) on a fixed prompt;
#      the fp8-KV output must stay COHERENT (no token salad, no degenerate loops)
#      and semantically match. MLA fp8 latent error is amplified by the kv_b_proj
#      up-projection, so a model that is fine with dense fp8-KV can still degrade
#      here — this is the specific thing to watch.
#   2. Confirm the fnuz path: GLM's AutoRound checkpoint is NOT fp8-calibrated, so
#      the KV fp8 uses runtime maxabs on Gaudi-2 fnuz (FP8_MAX=240). If a
#      QUANT_CONFIG minted elsewhere (Gaudi3, 448) is used, scale_adjustment must
#      rescale ±448->±240 (hpu_compressed_tensors.py:_update_scale_adjustment_if_
#      needed / fp8_max_original 448-vs-240) — verify the startup log shows the
#      G2 fnuz adjustment, else the latent-K clips.
#   3. With DSA (HPU_DSA_READY=1) the sparse indexer reads the latent cache; the
#      indexer's own K cache is bf16/uint8 (separate from the MLA latent) — fp8_inc
#      applies to the MLA latent only, so re-run the DSA recall/coherence check
#      (indexer recall ~0.99) with fp8 KV on to confirm the sparse path is unharmed.
#
# ============================================================================
# LAUNCH (same as glm51ar-lazy.env):  ./serve.sh glm51ar-fused-fp8kv
# Then push context/concurrency (the lever this profile adds): raise
# --max-model-len and/or --max-num-seqs vs the bf16-KV profile and watch HBM.
# Fall back to glm51ar-lazy.env if the MLA fp8-KV coherence gate fails.
# ============================================================================
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=GLM-5.1-int4-mixed-AutoRound
SERVED_NAME=glm51ar
# Base env == glm51ar-lazy.env MODEL_ENV (lazy + lazy-collectives + repack-load +
# the GLM coherence fixes + routed-K fused MoE) PLUS nothing else here — the fp8
# KV is a VLLM_ARGS flag, not an env. QUANT_CONFIG stays UNSET (case (a)); uncomment
# it (and mint maxabs_quant_g2.json first, on the g2 cards) for calibrated KV scales.
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1 -e PT_HPU_ENABLE_LAZY_COLLECTIVES=true -e HPU_MOE_REPACK_LOAD=/models/moe_repack_cache -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=1800 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e HPU_DSA_READY=1 -e HPU_SANITIZE_EMBED=1 -e HPU_GLM_ROPE_NEOX=1 -e MAX_EXPERTS_PER_SLICE=64 -e VLLM_DECODE_BS_BUCKET_MIN=1 -e HPU_MOE_ROUTED_K=8 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.1 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true"
# -e QUANT_CONFIG=/models/maxabs_quant_g2.json   # <- uncomment for CALIBRATED fp8 KV (case (b)); mint on the g2 cards first
#
# --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc is THE fp8-KV toggle (the only Gaudi-accepted KV dtype).
# --block-size 128 is the bf16/MME answer; the fp8-KV optimum is unverified (PRs
# #1453/#1461) — keep 128 to start, A/B if pushing long ctx. max-model-len here is
# RAISED vs the 512 of glm51ar-lazy.env because the ~2x KV headroom is the entire
# point of this profile; if the lazy prefill graph buffer OOMs at this length,
# lower it (the KV win is in bytes/token, independent of the chosen length).
VLLM_ARGS="--tensor-parallel-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --max-model-len 2048 --max-num-seqs 64 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
